    <string name="help_aa_off">Turn off Android Auto.</string>
    <string name="help_aa_off_detail">Disable or uninstall the Android Auto app, so the car talks to Gearslip instead.</string>
    <string name="help_cert">Load a certificate.</string>
    <string name="help_cert_detail">In Settings, download one or import your own.</string>
    <string name="help_mic">Allow the microphone.</string>
    <string name="help_mic_detail">Android won\'t let an app pass music to the car without it. Gearslip listens only when you tap the mic or press the talk button on your wheel.</string>
    <string name="help_plug_in">Plug in, or connect wirelessly.</string>
    <string name="help_plug_in_detail">Gearslip opens by itself when the car connects. For wireless, pair the phone with the car first, then tap Connect wirelessly on Home.</string>
    <string name="help_pair">Pair over Bluetooth for calls.</string>
    <string name="help_pair_detail">Calls play through the car once your phone and the car are paired. Gearslip offers to pair the first time you plug in.</string>
    <string name="help_answer">Answer calls from the car screen.</string>
    <string name="help_answer_detail">Set Gearslip as your caller ID and spam app. Without it, calls still ring, but only the phone can answer them.</string>
    <string name="help_prompt">Stop the audio prompt each drive.</string>
    <string name="help_prompt_detail">Connect the phone to a computer with USB debugging on, and run this once. Skip it and you tap Start each time you set off.</string>
    <string name="help_readable">Keep notifications readable.</string>
    <string name="help_readable_detail">Android hides what notifications say while it shares audio. Run this too, and Gearslip lifts that only while music goes to the car.</string>
    <string name="help_which_cars_body">Most cars work. Starting around 2020, some cars added newer security standards that reject Gearslip\'s certificate, and Gearslip can\'t run in those cars.</string>

